[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own table already
disagrees. Read by what each report describes, #4471 holds three problems. A parser fix closes
only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close the reports in #4471 when the parser fix ships. Two of the problems below survive it.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/mikolajadamski/support-desk-reports/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/mikolajadamski/support-desk-reports/issues/2',
    'one-day': 'https://github.com/mikolajadamski/support-desk-reports/issues/3',
  }}
/>

The export comes in overlapping pages, so some reports appear twice. Every count here is one
report per id, counted the way the desk counts: by tenant, so the one-day moves stay in the
`parser` count where the desk filed them, and have their own row too.

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first, so any date with both numbers at 12 or less flips: 7 April becomes 4 July. This is what
#4471 says it is.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form asks for the wrong order.** The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its
date field. People type what it asks, and the form reads the date day first. The dates flip
before they reach the parser. Only booking-v3 tenants, and only reports sent through the form.
The parser fix does not touch this.

**`one-day`: dates move by one day.** These are not flips: 12 May shows as 11 May, Lisbon and
Toronto get different days for one meeting, an invite arrives before its booking. The desk
listed them in `desk-notes.json` and counts them under the parser by tenant; they need their own fix. They look
like a time zone bug. One reporter says they stopped reporting it, so this count is a floor.

## Why it was one ticket

- Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser. The cause depends on the tenant: where they
  are and which booking form they run. The tags disagree with the cause on dozens of reports.
- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. Every subject in
  #4471 is some form of "wrong date", so subject cannot tell these problems apart.
- The #4471 table below shows the `hint` row as "no ticket of its own" and footnotes the
  one-day moves. Both were visible on the page; neither got a ticket.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- Count a merged ticket by what its reports describe, not by its subject or intake tag.
- Keep #4471 for the parser. Send new booking-v3 form reports to the `hint` ticket, and any
  "one day off" report to the `one-day` ticket.

